From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 18:29:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] docs(g6_03): feature bitmap after the 0xC2 MAC, opcode
 allocation rules, 0xD_ panel-fleet block (0xD0/0xD1 panel inventory)

The 0xC2 capability byte is full once ai_cal (bit 6) and health (bit 7,
already deployed) are both registered, so new command families are
advertised in a feature bitmap appended after the MAC. Its presence is
signalled by payload length -- the same tolerant extension the MAC uses --
so it needs no capability bit, which resolves the cap_ext vs health bit-7
conflict. Initial bits: panel_inventory, qwiic_i2c (replacing blind probing
of 0xB0), ai_stream (reserved).

Writes down general allocation rules (functional blocks; set on the even
code and get on the next odd code; legacy irregular pairs grandfathered)
with a block map of free codes, and opens 0xD_ as the panel-fleet block
with panel-inventory-scan / get-panel-inventory (presence + per-panel
firmware fingerprint) and the boot inventory sequence.

